  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nHigh pressure over the southwest states will be strongest on\nSaturday, then will slowly weaken into the middle of next week,\nbut with increasing lower level moisture and humidity for the\nearly and middle portion of next week for inland areas.\n\nHigh pressure will be strongest over southern California on\nSaturday. High temperatures on Saturday will be a few degrees\nwarmer than Friday, around 8 to 12 degrees above average for the\nmountains, deserts, and inland valleys. High temperatures on\nSaturday will range from around 80 near the coast to the upper 90s\nto 108 for the Inland Empire with 116 to 120 for the lower\ndeserts. \n\nHigh temperatures will cool a few degrees on Sunday and cool a few\nto around 5 degrees on Monday with the greatest cooling on Monday\nin the San Diego County valleys. Not much change is expected on\nTuesday. High temperatures on Monday and Tuesday will range from a\nfew degrees above average near the coast to 5 to 10 degrees above\naverage for the mountains and deserts. High temperatures for\nMonday and Tuesday will range from the mid 70s to around 80 near \nthe coast to the mid 90s to 105 for the Inland Empire with 114 to\n118 for the lower deserts. There will be widespread extreme\nHeatRisk for the lower deserts for Sunday through Tuesday.",
